    "updated_at": "2021-10-13T02:05:45Z",
    "body": "This occurs because it takes time for git to get information from your current repository.\r\n\r\nIf you're okay with having all information except for git status (e.g. # stashed, dirty, untracked, etc.), you can disable the git status module by adding\r\n\r\n```\r\n[git_status]\r\ndisabled=true\r\n```\r\n\r\ninto your `starship.toml`. If you want to allow git to run for longer periods without timing out, you can raise the `command_timeout` to something like `1000` (default is `500` for 500ms), but this could potentially slow down the prompt drawing speed.",
